        ],
        "text": "@JacoblAmi1 @ycombinator @spacexai @poteto @romanugarte_ You're right that purpose-built APIs are cleaner long-term. Computer use is just temporary scaffolding so agents can deliver value today on the huge pile of existing human software that won't get rewritten overnight. Native tools get built in parallel, but waiting for purity"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "1206292044622245892",
        "created_at": "2026-11-15T00:36:42.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
